   "definition_quote": "We consider an unknown reward function $f:\\calA \\rightarrow \\bbR$ lying in the reproducing kernel Hilbert space (RKHS) $\\mathcal{H}$ associated with a given kernel $K$, i.e., $f(x) = \\langle f, K(x,\\cdot) \\rangle_{K}$. Similar to the linear bandit setting, we assume that $\\max_{x \\in \\calA} |f(x)| \\le 1$ and $\\|f\\|_K \\le b$ for some $b > 0$. \n\n\nAt each round $t=1,2,\\dots,T$,\nthe learner chooses an action $x_t\\in\\calA \\subseteq [0, 1]^d$ and observes the reward\n\\[\n    y_t \\;=\\; f(x_t) \\;+\\; \\eta_t,\n\\]\nwhere $\\eta_t$ are independent noise terms that satisfy $\\mathbb{E}[\\eta_t]=0$ and\n$\\mathbb{E}\\bigl[|\\eta_t|^{1+\\epsilon}\\bigr]\\le\\upsilon$"
